1lfa|n|A plant common in Europe (Paris quadrifolia); herb Paris; truelove. It has been used as a narcotic. ; The chief city of France.	a:1gfu,59,3;1jsv,42,3~1gfu,59,3;1jsv,42,3	n:qq7,137,4;jhm,72,3~qq7,137,4;jhm,72,3	N:vtk,54,1~vtk,54,1
1lfm|n|The quality or condition of being equal or equivalent; A like state or degree; equality; close correspondence; analogy; as, parity of reasoning.	n:x6r,89,3~x6r,89,3
1lfo|n|A piece of ground inclosed, and stored with beasts of the chase, which a man may have by prescription, or the king's grant. ; A tract of ground kept in its natural state, about or adjacent to a residence, as for the preservation of game, for walking, riding, or the like. ; A piece of ground, in or near a city or town, inclosed and kept for ornament and recreation; as, Hyde Park in London; Central Park in New York. ; A space occupied by the animals, wagons, pontoons, and materials of all kinds, as ammunition, ordnance stores, hospital stores, provisions, etc., when brought together; also, the objects themselves; as, a park of wagons; a park of artillery. ; A partially inclosed basin in which oysters are grown.	a:22qn,89,5~22qn,89,5	v:22qn,66,1~22qn,66,1	n:6oo,101,12;22qn,92,6;f01,60,8~6oo,101,12;f01,60,8;22qn,92,6	N:7qs,96,2;1pnh,23,2~7qs,96,2;1pnh,23,2
1lfo|v|To inclose in a park, or as in a park. ; To bring together in a park, or compact body; as, to park the artillery, the wagons, etc.	o:1pnh,13,1~1pnh,13,1	s:22qn,66,1~22qn,66,1
1lfo|a|A piece of ground inclosed, and stored with beasts of the chase, which a man may have by prescription, or the king's grant. ; A tract of ground kept in its natural state, about or adjacent to a residence, as for the preservation of game, for walking, riding, or the like. ; A piece of ground, in or near a city or town, inclosed and kept for ornament and recreation; as, Hyde Park in London; Central Park in New York. ; A space occupied by the animals, wagons, pontoons, and materials of all kinds, as ammunition, ordnance stores, hospital stores, provisions, etc., when brought together; also, the objects themselves; as, a park of wagons; a park of artillery. ; A partially inclosed basin in which oysters are grown.	j:1pnh,29,3~1pnh,29,3
