1lky|n|The state or condition of being a partner; as, to be in partnership with another; to have partnership in the fortunes of a family or a state. ; A division or sharing among partners; joint possession or interest. ; An alliance or association of persons for the prosecution of an undertaking or a business on joint account; a company; a firm; a house; as, to form a partnership. ; A contract between two or more competent persons for joining together their money, goods, labor, and skill, or any or all of them, under an understanding that there shall be a communion of profit between them, and for the purpose of carrying on a legal trade, business, or adventure. ; See Fellowship, n., 6.	a:e1z,85,3~e1z,85,3	n:1vkx,19,4~1vkx,19,4
